# The ship editor (ShipEdit and HangarTab, scripts/shipedit/shipedit.py and hangartab.py, issue #2): the tabs, the
# background and the Hangar panel. The C functions (src/game/Script/ShipEdit.c) pick a section and give the values:
#   $mp      ShipEdit.IsEditingMultiplayer() (a network game or the ShipEdit level: the pilots, no money)
#   $sputnik ShipEdit.fromSputnik (the hangar screen of Sputnik: pick a ship, no editing)
#   $xbox    HangarTab.isXbox
# The step "run use <Attr> <key> [item]" sets the attribute to the language text key formatted with UseTxt (the click
# or button text of the script module), "run sputnikhint <n>" the hint of a hangar on Sputnik's screen (it computes
# the rebuild cost), "run ramp" the place of SpeedRamp2 (the width of SpeedRamp1 times its scale).

# ---- ShipEdit.AddShipEditTabs: one tab; $name ShipEditTab<tab>, $text its title, $x the left of the tab,
# $init and $end its quads, $first the first tab, $only the only tab (Sputnik)
section tab
item $(name) Text
	IsMultiSprite 1
	File 2D/ShipEditor/hangar.alpha.tga
	Font ScrapMedium
	FocusSpriteIndex 33
	Text $text
	Alpha 255
	if $tab == Hangar
		Red 255
		Green 234
		Blue 177
	else
		Red 170.0
		Green 156.0
		Blue 118.0
	end
	X $x+6
	Y 28
	W 114
	H 42
	if $tab == Hangar
		SpriteIndex 41
		Highlight 1
		TextColorAlpha 255
		TextColorRed 255
		TextColorGreen 255
		TextColorBlue 255
		OnAccept ShipEdit.ChangeTab
		Hint "{HINT_Tabs1}"
		if $only
			OnAccept ""
		end
	else
		SpriteIndex 18
		Highlight 0
		Alpha 255
		TextColorAlpha 255
		TextColorRed 161
		TextColorGreen 161
		TextColorBlue 161
		OnAccept ""
		if $tab == Engines
			run use Hint HINT_Tabs6
		elif $tab == Weapons
			run use Hint HINT_Tabs7
		else
			run use Hint HINT_Tabs8
		end
	end
item Tab_$(name) Tab
	call Menu.SetTabDefaults $id Tab_$(name)
	X 47
	Y 37
	SizeX 546
	SizeY 406
	TabInit $init
	TabEnd $end
	TabMax 64
	SizeTabQuad 3
	Filled 0
	if $first
		Type 0
		Alpha 1
		Red 57
		Green 139
		Blue 202
	else
		Type 1
		Alpha 192
		Red 20
		Green 60
		Blue 160
	end

